---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { business as b } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="The Studio: A Marsh-View Recording Sanctuary in St. Augustine | The Fish Tank"
  description="An elevated recording studio down a private drive overlooking the St. Augustine marsh, with a huge deck, an SSL Origin console and a FLEA U47. A sanctuary for artists since 2002."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'The Studio', path: '/studio/' }]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About · The sanctuary" title="Where the music meets <em>the marsh.</em>"
    lede={`The Fish Tank sits at the end of a private drive in St. Augustine, Fla., in an elevated space that looks out over the marsh. The tubes are warm, the coffee is on and the view runs for miles. Since ${b.founded}, it has served as a retreat where artists collaborate and reconnect with their music, and with a little quiet.`} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="gallery">
        <img class="img img--wide g1" src="/images/control-room-wide.webp" alt="The Fish Tank control room with an SSL console and a wall of guitars" width="1080" height="607" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g2" src="/images/vocal-booth.webp" alt="The vocal booth at The Fish Tank" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g3" src="/images/live-room.webp" alt="The live room at The Fish Tank, with amps, drums and a red rug" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g4" src="/images/manley-closeup.webp" alt="Close-up of Manley outboard gear with glowing VU meters" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A sanctuary, <em>not a booking room.</em></h2>
        <p>Many studios are windowless rooms in industrial parks. The Fish Tank has a wide view of the St. Augustine marsh, with wading birds over the grass, the tide moving in and out, and long Florida sunsets.</p>
        <p>A large deck sits just outside the control room. Artists step out between takes to clear their heads or talk through a bridge, then go back in to track. For Rubino, that pace is the point: sessions here are built around connection, to the song, to the other people in the room and to the setting.</p>

        <h2>Built for <em>making records.</em></h2>
        <p>Rubino designed the studio as part of the creative process. Songs get written on the couch, vocals get coached in the live room, and records are tracked, mixed and mastered without leaving the property.</p>
        <p>The control room is built around an <strong>SSL Origin</strong> console feeding <strong>Pro Tools HD</strong>, with outboard from Shadow Hills, Elysia, API, Empirical Labs and A-Designs. The vocal chain starts with a <strong>FLEA U47 Next</strong>, a modern build of the classic Neumann U47 design, and Royer and AEA ribbon mics cover guitars and room sound. Personal monitor mixes let a five-piece band track together.</p>
        <p>The instrument collection includes a wall of basses (Fender P-Bass, Music Man StingRay fretless, Dingwall, Zon and a six-string), guitars from Collings, PRS and Taylor, an upright bass, a Dobro, a banjo-guitar and a Medicine Man drum kit.</p>
        <p><a href="/gear/">Full gear list →</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Visit</p>
        <h3>{b.street}<br />{b.city}, {b.region} {b.postal}</h3>
        <p>Private drive · marsh-view deck · sessions by appointment</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a session →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .gallery { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .g1 { grid-column: 1 / -1; aspect-ratio: 21/9; }
  .g2, .g3, .g4 { aspect-ratio: 4/5; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .gallery { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .g1 { aspect-ratio: 16/10; } }
</style>
